916: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
917: // 5. TRANSACTION — PREPARE / RECORD / FINALIZE
918: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
919: //
920: // runDivergentPivot works only when the caller can hand it a synchronous,
921: // in-process dispatchSeat callback. A YAML-interpreted workflow cannot:
922: // only the running agent can natively dispatch a Council seat, and a
923: // single script invocation cannot pause mid-run for that and resume with
924: // the result. The three functions below split the same transaction across
925: // process boundaries — prepare persists everything up through "which seats
926: // are still missing" and returns; recordPivotSeatResult durably records
927: // one externally-obtained seat result per call (one per native dispatch
928: // step); finalize re-derives all context from disk (via the durable
929: // config.json prepare already wrote) and completes the transaction.
930: // runDivergentPivot composes all three for callers that do have a working
931: // synchronous dispatchSeat, so its observable behavior is unchanged.
932: 
